.TH BITCHAT-LAUNCHER 1 "October 2026" "bitchat-launcher 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bitchat-launcher \- the BitChat map (bitchat-geohash) with the console (bitchat-console) over it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bitchat-launcher
.I geohash
.RB [ \-\-teleport ]
.RB [ \-\-map\-geohash
.IR gh ]
.RB [ \-\-depth
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-open ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-tor\-socks
.I addr:port
.RB "| " \-\-arti ]
.RB [ \-\-tls\-cert
.I pem
.B \-\-tls\-key
.I pem
.RB "| " \-\-http ]
.RB [ \-\-console\-args
.IR args ]
.RB [ \-\-map\-args
.IR args ]
.RB [ \-\-console\-bin
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-map\-bin
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-data\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.br
.B bitchat-launcher
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-man " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bitchat-launcher
starts two programs together and stops them together:
.TP
.B bitchat-geohash
the live map of BitChat location\-channel activity: for each channel of an area, it
listens on the relays the iOS and Android apps choose, read\-only, and shows counts per cell.
.TP
.B bitchat-console
a BitChat client for location channels: it follows a cell and its 8 neighbours through Tor,
writes there, and talks in private and in groups. With the map, it serves the map's page
with the console floating over it; a cell of the map can be followed in one click, and when
the console follows another cell, the map watches the area around it (its parent) with
bitchat-geohash 0.2.0 or later. The map's own panel can also change the watched area.
.PP
The launcher picks the ports, finds a working Tor, makes the HTTPS certificate, starts the
map on a loopback port of its own and the console on the page's port, waits until both
answer, and opens
.BI https://localhost: port /
in the browser. Lines of the tools are printed with
.B [map]
or
.B [console]
in front. Ctrl\-C (or SIGTERM) stops the console, then the map, each with SIGINT and
20 seconds to finish (then SIGKILL). If one tool stops on its own, the other is stopped too.
.SH OPTIONS
The most used first.
.TP
.I geohash
The cell the console follows, with its 8 neighbours (for example
.BR u09tv ).
.TP
.B \-\-teleport
You are not in that place: the console tags its messages as teleported and sends no
presence, like a teleported user of the app. Without it, it sends presences.
.TP
.BI \-\-map\-geohash " gh"
The area of the map. Default: the console's geohash without its last letter
.RB ( u09tv " gives " u09t ),
so that the map shows the cells around the one followed.
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " n"
How many channel levels the map watches below its area (the map's
.BR \-\-depth ;
its default is 1).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
Do not open the browser; the address is printed.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " n"
Port of the page, on 127.0.0.1. Default: 8080 if free, else a free port between 50000 and
60000. A port given here must be free: there is no fallback. The map gets another free port
of that range, on 127.0.0.1, reached by the console only.
.TP
.BI \-\-tor\-socks " addr:port"
The Tor daemon's SOCKS port the console uses. It must work: there is no fallback.
.TP
.B \-\-arti
The Tor inside bitchat-console (Arti), which must be built with
.BR "\-\-features arti" .
.TP
.BI \-\-tls\-cert " pem " \-\-tls\-key " pem"
The page's certificate and private key, instead of the one the launcher makes.
.TP
.B \-\-http
Clear HTTP on the loopback instead of HTTPS. The browser then keeps at most 6 connections
to the page, one per live view.
.TP
.BI \-\-console\-args " args"
More options for bitchat-console (see
.BR "CONSOLE OPTIONS" ),
in one argument split like a shell does:
.B \-\-console\-args \(aq\-\-pow\-bits 12 \-\-no\-presence\(aq.
May be repeated. The options the launcher sets are refused:
.BR \-\-listen ", " \-\-allow\-remote ", " \-\-tls\-cert ", " \-\-tls\-key ", " \-\-map ,
.BR \-\-tor\-socks ", " \-\-arti ", " \-\-open .
.TP
.BI \-\-map\-args " args"
More options for bitchat-geohash (see
.BR "MAP OPTIONS" ),
the same way. Refused:
.BR \-\-listen ", " \-\-allow\-remote ", " \-\-insecure\-remote ", " \-\-tls\-cert ,
.BR \-\-tls\-key ", " \-\-open .
They come after the launcher's own, so a
.B \-\-db
given here wins.
.TP
.BI \-\-console\-bin " path"
.TQ
.BI \-\-map\-bin " path"
The binaries. Default: next to the launcher's binary, else on
.BR $PATH .
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " dir"
Where the launcher keeps the certificate
.RI ( dir /tls)
and the map's database
.RI ( dir /bitchat-geohash.sqlite).
Default:
.BR ~/.bitchat-launcher ,
readable by you only. The console keeps its keys in its own directory (its
.BR \-\-data\-dir ).
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Both tools log in detail.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
The options, briefly.
.TP
.B \-\-man
This manual.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
The launcher's version.
.SH CONSOLE OPTIONS
Options of
.B bitchat-console
that go in
.BR \-\-console\-args .
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " dir"
Keys (device seed, Noise identity) and local storage (muted keys, saved and scheduled
messages). Default:
.BR ~/.bitchat-console .
Files are created readable by you only; files readable by others are refused.
.TP
.BI \-\-relays\-csv " url|path"
The iOS relay list (geohash and coordinates of each relay). Default: the app's official list,
downloaded through Tor, with a cached copy if the download fails.
.TP
.BI \-\-android\-csv " url|path"
The Android relay list. Default: the Android app's official list.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-android
No Android list: only the iOS choice of relays.
.TP
.BR \-\-apps " both|ios|android"
Whose choice of relays is used for each cell: both apps' (default, the union), or one.
.TP
.BI \-\-dm\-relays " url,url"
Relays of private messages. Default: the apps' default relays.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-presence
Send no presence, even when not teleported.
.TP
.BI \-\-pow\-bits " n"
Proof of work on sent messages, 0 to 32 bits (default 8, as the iOS app). It is computed for
2 seconds at most, then the target is halved.
.TP
.B \-\-teleport
Same as the launcher's
.BR \-\-teleport .
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Detailed logs of the console only.
.PP
Set by the launcher:
.B \-\-listen
(the page's port),
.B \-\-map
(the map),
.BR \-\-tor\-socks / \-\-arti ,
.BR \-\-tls\-cert / \-\-tls\-key .
.SH MAP OPTIONS
Options of
.B bitchat-geohash
that go in
.BR \-\-map\-args .
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " n"
Channel levels watched below the area (default 1). Same as the launcher's
.BR \-\-depth .
.TP
.BI \-\-levels " 2,4,5,6"
Channel levels shown (2 region, 4 province, 5 city, 6 neighbourhood, 7 block).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-cells " n"
Most channels watched at once (default 2048); a bigger area is refused.
.TP
.BI \-\-window " 15m"
Counting window of messages and participants (90, 90s, 15m, 2h).
.TP
.BI \-\-inactivity " 15m"
A watched channel without any event for this long is retired (it can be reinstated from the
map).
.TP
.BI \-\-relays\-csv " url|path"
.TQ
.BI \-\-android\-csv " url|path"
.TQ
.B \-\-no\-android
Relay lists, as for the console.
.TP
.B \-\-reload\-lists
Download the relay lists at start. Otherwise lists loaded less than 24 hours ago from the
same sources are taken from the map's database (bitchat-geohash 0.2.1 or later).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-probe
Do not probe the relays before listening (dead relays are then listened to as well).
.TP
.BI \-\-db " path"
The map's database (relay probes, retired channels, descents). Default with the launcher:
.IR data-dir /bitchat-geohash.sqlite.
.TP
.B \-\-reinstate\-all
Watch again the channels retired in a previous run.
.TP
.B \-\-forget\-descents
Do not restore the channels added by descents in previous runs, and forget them.
.TP
.BI \-\-tiles " url " \-\-tiles\-attribution " html"
Other map tiles, with their provider's credit (default: OpenStreetMap).
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Detailed logs of the map only.
.PP
Set by the launcher:
.BR \-\-listen ;
the map is served in clear HTTP on the loopback, to the console only.
.SH TOR
The console never connects to a relay without Tor. Unless
.B \-\-tor\-socks
or
.B \-\-arti
is given, the launcher tries in order:
.IP 1. 4
the SOCKS port in
.BR $BITCHAT_TOR_SOCKS ;
.IP 2. 4
the Tor daemon's default port, 127.0.0.1:9050;
.IP 3. 4
Arti, inside bitchat-console.
.PP
A daemon counts as working when it takes a SOCKS user name (the console isolates each cell
on its own circuit by user name) and opens a stream to check.torproject.org:443 within 30
seconds. With Arti, the console bootstraps Tor itself (a few seconds, longer the first time).
To install the daemon on macOS:
.B brew install tor
then
.B tor
or
.BR "brew services start tor" .
.PP
The map does not use Tor: it connects to the relays directly, read\-only (it never publishes).
The browser loads the map tiles directly too.
.SH HTTPS
Over HTTP/1.1 a browser keeps at most 6 connections per host, and each live view (map, console)
holds one; HTTPS brings HTTP/2, without that limit. By default the launcher makes, once, a
certificate for localhost, 127.0.0.1 and ::1 with
.BR mkcert ,
in
.IR data-dir /tls
(key readable by you only). The browser trusts it when mkcert's authority is installed:
.BR "brew install mkcert && mkcert \-install" ,
once.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BITCHAT_TOR_SOCKS
A Tor daemon's SOCKS port
.RI ( addr:port ),
tried first.
.TP
.B PATH
Where the tools are looked for when they are not next to the launcher.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.bitchat-launcher/tls/cert.pem, key.pem
The page's certificate.
.TP
.B ~/.bitchat-launcher/bitchat-geohash.sqlite
The map's database.
.TP
.B ~/.bitchat-console/
The console's keys and storage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after Ctrl\-C or SIGTERM; 1 when a tool cannot start, does not answer within 5 minutes, or
stops on its own; 2 for a wrong command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B bitchat-launcher u09tv \-\-teleport
Follow #u09tv and its neighbours as a teleported user, over the map of #u09t.
.TP
.B bitchat-launcher u09tv \-\-map\-geohash u09 \-\-depth 2
A wider map: #u09, two levels down.
.TP
.B BITCHAT_TOR_SOCKS=127.0.0.1:9150 bitchat-launcher u09tv
Through Tor Browser's port when it is open.
.TP
.B bitchat-launcher u09tv \-\-console\-args \(aq\-\-apps ios \-\-pow\-bits 12\(aq \-\-map\-args \(aq\-\-no\-probe\(aq
Options of each tool.
.SH PRIVACY
Received messages, nicknames and keys stay in the console's memory; nothing about other people
is written to disk or to the logs, except the keys you mute. The map gets counts only. Both
pages are served on the loopback only.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bitchat-console " (README.md, SPECIFICATIONS.md),"
.BR bitchat-geohash " (README.md),"
.BR tor (1),
.BR mkcert (1).
